WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.281 --> 00:00:18.144
When Jason walked into the gym, Miss Shelly was putting up a sign.

2
00:00:19.165 --> 00:00:22.347
It said: "Donations for Liberty Elementary."

3
00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:26.470
There were empty cardboard boxes lined up beneath the sign.

4
00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:28.311
"What's going on?"

5
00:00:28.751 --> 00:00:29.332
he asked.

6
00:00:30.552 --> 00:00:34.355
"An elementary school burned down after last week's lightning storm.

7
00:00:35.276 --> 00:00:38.939
Those kids lost all their books, pencils everything!

8
00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:42.943
Now they need lots of help," Miss Shelly said.

9
00:00:45.004 --> 00:00:47.867
Jason pulled a brand-new eraser out of his pocket.

10
00:00:47.887 --> 00:00:50.969
"Here," he said.

11
00:00:50.989 --> 00:00:52.771
"Our first donation."

12
00:00:52.791 --> 00:00:54.933
"Thanks, Jason.

13
00:00:55.813 --> 00:00:58.376
That's very sweet," Miss Shelly said.

14
00:01:01.548 --> 00:01:04.269
"Mr. Frick told us about this today," Ethan said.

15
00:01:04.289 --> 00:01:07.110
"I'm going to bring my old calculator tomorrow."

16
00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:11.911
"I'm sure the kids would like any donations," Miss Shelly said.

17
00:01:11.931 --> 00:01:15.012
"But we'll talk more about it later.

18
00:01:16.152 --> 00:01:17.552
Now put on your aprons!

19
00:01:18.493 --> 00:01:21.854
We're making applesauce muffins," Miss Shelly said.

20
00:01:28.015 --> 00:01:29.816
we need to mix the dry ingredients.

21
00:01:30.804 --> 00:01:32.926
Bobby, show Ethan how we do it."

22
00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:37.650
"One and a half cups flour," Bobby read from the easel.

23
00:01:49.159 --> 00:01:51.741
powder and baking soda," Jason continued.

24
00:01:55.484 --> 00:01:58.386
half teaspoon of salt," Nina read next.

25
00:01:59.227 --> 00:02:00.308
Everyone looked at Ethan.

26
00:02:01.908 --> 00:02:03.270
"Cinnamon!" he said.

27
00:02:07.954 --> 00:02:11.378
Now we mix the wet ingredients," Miss Shelly said.

28
00:02:11.398 --> 00:02:15.081
"Melted butter," Izzie said.

29
00:02:20.066 --> 00:02:22.528
of a cup brown sugar," Bobby said.

30
00:02:22.548 --> 00:02:25.611
"Mix well."

31
00:02:28.824 --> 00:02:31.906
"Two eggs," Jason said, cracking an egg.

32
00:02:31.926 --> 00:02:36.950
"One and a half cups applesauce," Ethan read.

33
00:02:42.033 --> 00:02:44.154
we mix the wet and dry together.

34
00:02:44.935 --> 00:02:46.196
But just a little bit.

35
00:02:47.036 --> 00:02:51.199
Too much mixing is not good for muffin batter," Miss Shelly told them.

36
00:02:51.219 --> 00:02:54.602
"I'll pour the wet into the dry bowl.

37
00:02:55.542 --> 00:02:57.864
Ethan, you mix," Izzie said.

38
00:02:58.852 --> 00:03:01.694
"Izzie can be bossy," Bobby said to Ethan.

39
00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:04.776
"But she's nice."

40
00:03:07.217 --> 00:03:10.219
Everyone lined the muffin pan with colorful paper cups.

41
00:03:11.319 --> 00:03:14.141
"Now we pour in the batter," Miss Shelly said.

42
00:03:14.161 --> 00:03:16.782
"But don't fill the cups completely.

43
00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:19.284
The muffins will rise in the oven."

44
00:03:27.244 --> 00:03:28.525
"How long do we bake them for?"

45
00:03:28.945 --> 00:03:29.705
Izzie asked.

46
00:03:30.666 --> 00:03:32.807
"Twenty minutes," Miss Shelly said.

47
00:03:37.249 --> 00:03:40.711
Jason was thinking about the kids at Liberty Elementary again.

48
00:03:40.731 --> 00:03:44.753
"Do the Liberty kids have an after-school program?"

49
00:03:45.054 --> 00:03:45.654
he asked.

50
00:03:47.175 --> 00:03:48.215
Miss Shelly nodded.

51
00:03:48.235 --> 00:03:52.838
"Their program is meeting in the town hall until the school is fixed."

52
00:03:52.858 --> 00:03:55.499
"Do they need donations too?"

53
00:03:55.859 --> 00:03:56.820
Jason asked.

54
00:03:58.088 --> 00:04:01.609
"Yes, they lost most of their craft and cooking supplies.

55
00:04:02.629 --> 00:04:05.310
It will be tough for a while," Miss Shelly said.

56
00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:09.671
"I wish there was something else we could do," Jason thought.

57
00:04:09.691 --> 00:04:13.112
"The muffins are ready!"

58
00:04:13.512 --> 00:04:15.973
Izzie cried, running to the toaster oven.

59
00:04:20.654 --> 00:04:24.015
they cool a little, we can try them," Miss Shelly said.

60
00:04:24.035 --> 00:04:26.155
"Wait! Don't eat them!"

61
00:04:26.556 --> 00:04:27.816
Jason said suddenly.

62
00:04:28.692 --> 00:04:29.812
"I have an idea!"

63
00:04:29.832 --> 00:04:34.214
"We should give our muffins to Liberty's after-school program!"

64
00:04:34.554 --> 00:04:35.334
Jason said.

65
00:04:35.354 --> 00:04:38.776
"We can call them after-school applesauce muffins!"

66
00:04:38.796 --> 00:04:41.496
"Great idea!"

67
00:04:41.837 --> 00:04:42.737
Miss Shelly said.

68
00:04:42.757 --> 00:04:45.318
"We can deliver them tomorrow."

69
00:04:45.338 --> 00:04:47.278
"All right!"

70
00:04:47.619 --> 00:04:48.639
Jason cheered.

71
00:04:49.619 --> 00:04:51.160
It felt good to help others.
